.TH XUR.STD.ASSERT 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.assert \- test assertions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::assert;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::assert
provides assertion functions for testing. Each function
panics with a descriptive message when the assertion fails.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B is_eq(left, right)
Assert that
.I left
equals
.IR right .
.TP
.B is_ne(left, right)
Assert that
.I left
does not equal
.IR right .
.TP
.B is_true(value)
Assert that
.I value
is
.BR true .
.TP
.B is_false(value)
Assert that
.I value
is
.BR false .
.TP
.B fail(message)
Unconditionally fail with
.IR message .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::assert;

fn main() {
    assert::is_eq(1 + 1, 2);
    assert::is_ne("hello", "world");
    assert::is_true(10 > 5);
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7)
